module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Completion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsCompletion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.LocalCalculation
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.IdealSubsheafLocal
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many global sections

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪`. This file
constructs the sheaf of ideals `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪` they generate and proves the API its
consumers need. It is the `ℐ` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] — "let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` be the ideal sheaf generated
by `f_1, …, f_r`" — which until now could not be written down, so that both that tag and
[Stacks, Tag 099F] could only be *stated* at an arbitrary sheaf of ideals.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presheafGeneratedIdeal`: the objectwise ideal
  `U ↦ (f_1|_U, …, f_r|_U) ⊂ 𝒪(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf`: **the sheaf of ideals generated by
  `f_1, …, f_r`**, the smallest sheaf of ideals containing the objectwise one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection`: a compatible family of local
  sections of `𝒪`, and a section over a terminal object of the site, read as global sections in
  the sense of [Stacks, Tag 06UN].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatingSections`: `ℐ` presented as generated by `r` global
  sections, together with the epimorphism `𝒪^r ⟶ ℐ`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.forall_globalSectionVal_mem_toSubmodule_generatedIdealSheaf`:
  each `f_i` is a section of `ℐ` over every object. The second is the same statement in the
  spelling in which consumers carry it as a hypothesis on an arbitrary sheaf of ideals, so that
  at `ℐ` the hypothesis is discharged with no bridge.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf_le`: `ℐ` is the smallest sheaf of ideals
  containing the `f_i`; with the previous result this characterises it, so a statement about
  `generatedIdealSheaf f` is a statement about the `ℐ` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] and nothing else.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff`: **the local description.** A
  section of `𝒪` over `V` lies in `ℐ` exactly when, along every arrow of some covering sieve of
  `V`, it becomes an `𝒪`-linear combination of the `f_i`. This is the property that the source's
  proofs use and that no leastness characterisation supplies.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf`: for `I ⊂ A` an
  ideal generated by finitely many elements and `ρ : A ⟶ Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)`, the sheaf of ideals generated
  by the images of the generators is the `I𝒪` of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy`, so that hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] is now satisfiable rather than merely assumable.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver_generatedIdealSheaf`: over
  a terminal object of the site, `ℐ` satisfies the generation hypothesis of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver`, the hypothesis
  [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] is stated at in `LocalCalculation.lean`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isLocallySurjective_generatingSectionsHom` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_generatingSections`: `ℐ` is generated, as a sheaf of
  modules, by `r` global sections — [Stacks, Tag 01B4] for `ℐ` — the generating family being
  finite.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf`: `ℐ` is of finite type in
  Mathlib's sense, `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, on a site over which that predicate can be
  unwound; see the implementation note.
* `RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_generatedIdealSheaf`: the
  reduction of [Stacks, Tag 099F] of `Completion.lean`, restated at the ideal sheaf `ℐ` generated
  by the `f_i` rather than at an arbitrary one.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.generatedIdealSheaf_eq_generatedIdeal`, in
  `GeneratedIdealSheafSpace.lean`: on the small Zariski site of a ringed space this construction
  agrees with `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.generatedIdeal`.

## Implementation notes

*Which presentation, and what the alternative would have cost.* `ℐ` is built as a **subsheaf of
the structure sheaf**: the objectwise ideal `U ↦ (f_1|_U, …, f_r|_U)` is formed first — it is
stable under restriction because the `f_i` are global sections, so a restriction of a
combination of them is a combination of them — and then `ℐ` is the smallest subsheaf of `𝒪`
containing it, `Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule`, whose membership condition is local.
The sections of that closure are described objectwise, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff`, as the sections lying in the objectwise ideal
locally, which is what gives `mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff`.

The alternative presentation is the **sheafified image of a map out of a free module**: take
`𝒪^r ⟶ 𝒪` with components multiplication by the `f_i` and let `ℐ` be its image. It would give the
generating sections for free, but its value is a quotient of `𝒪^r`, an object of
`SheafOfModules ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))` and not a
`SheafOfModules.Submodule (SheafOfModules.unit …)` — and the latter is the type that
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete` and [Stacks, Tag 099F] demand, a sheaf of ideals
being a *sub*object of `𝒪` there. Recovering the subobject from the quotient means computing the
image, which is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule` — the sections lying locally
in the pointwise range — that is, the same local condition, reached by a longer route. Going the
other way is cheap: the generating sections, below, are produced from the local description.

The two presentations also differ in what they make hard. The subsheaf presentation makes
leastness and the local description immediate and the generating sections work
(`isLocallySurjective_generatingSectionsHom`, which must exhibit a locally surjective map out of
`SheafOfModules.free`); the image presentation would reverse that. Since every consumer in this
directory needs a sheaf of ideals and three of them need the local description, the subsheaf
presentation wins.

*Why not `sInf` alone.* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.extendIdeal` of `RestrictScalars.lean` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.generatedIdeal` of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/
QuasiRegular/Basic.lean` both define a generated ideal sheaf as an infimum of the ideal sheaves
containing the generators. That is the same object — `generatedIdealSheaf_le` and
`globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf` say so, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.generatedIdealSheaf_eq_generatedIdeal` of
`GeneratedIdealSheafSpace.lean` makes the identification for the ringed-space one — but an
infimum carries no description of its sections beyond "lies in every upper bound", and every use
of `ℐ` in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is an argument about a local section of `ℐ` over an
arbitrary object. So the closure of the objectwise ideal is taken instead, and the infimum
characterisation is then a consequence rather than the definition.

*Global sections.* The index shape is `f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (𝒪 ⋙ forget)`, which
is the shape `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor` and the whole Čech development of
this directory are indexed by; `globalSectionVal` reads off the value over an object.
`globalSectionOfSections` converts from the other spelling of a global section used in this
directory, `RingCat.sectionsSubring`, which is what
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy` consumes.

*Finite type, and the two forms it takes.* Over the site itself what is proved is that `ℐ` is
generated by `r` *global* sections: `generatingSections`, whose index type is `ULift (Fin r)`, so
that `isFiniteType_generatingSections` holds. Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` is a
different, weaker statement — the existence of `SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData`, a covering
of the terminal object together with finite generating sections of the restriction of `ℐ` to each
member's slice site — and deducing it from global generators goes through
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.localGeneratorsData`, which carries `[HasBinaryProducts 𝒞]`,
`[∀ U, HasSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat]` and
`[∀ U, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat]`. Those are hypotheses on the *site*,
which [Stacks, Tag 099B] does not make, so `isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf` carries them
explicitly rather than their being hidden in a section variable; on a site without them the
statement available is the global generating family, which is the stronger of the two.

### What is *not* proved here

None of the three hypotheses `hΦ`, `hη`, `hcomm` of
`isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_generatedIdealSheaf` is discharged *here*: this
file supplies the ideal sheaf that reduction was missing, not the reduction's inputs. `hη` is
discharged downstream, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`
of `CompletionUnitInvertible.lean`, whose membership input is
`forall_globalSectionVal_mem_toSubmodule_generatedIdealSheaf` above; `hΦ` and `hcomm` remain
open. Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` attribute — [Stacks, Tag 099B] states the existence of
the left adjoint, and the construction of its `ℐ` is a step inside that statement, not a tag of
its own.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06UN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06UN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Objectwise

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The objectwise ideal generated by `f_1, …, f_r`**: over an object `U` of the site, the
ideal of `𝒪(U)` generated by the values of the global sections there. -/
def sectionSpan (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) : Ideal (X.O.obj.obj U) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ globalSectionVal (f i) U)

/-- The sections of the objectwise ideal over `U` are the `𝒪(U)`-linear combinations of the
values of `f_1, …, f_r` there. -/
theorem mem_sectionSpan_iff (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.O.obj.obj U) :
    x ∈ sectionSpan f U ↔
      ∃ c : Fin r → X.O.obj.obj U, ∑ i, c i * globalSectionVal (f i) U = x :=
  Ideal.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun

/-- The value of `f_i` over an object lies in the objectwise ideal there. -/
theorem globalSectionVal_mem_sectionSpan (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ sectionSpan f U :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-- Restriction carries the objectwise ideal into the objectwise ideal: the `f_i` being global
sections, the restriction of `∑ c_i f_i|_U` is `∑ c_i|_V f_i|_V`. -/
theorem map_mem_sectionSpan {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V) {x : X.O.obj.obj U}
    (hx : x ∈ sectionSpan f U) : (X.O.obj.map g).hom x ∈ sectionSpan f V := by
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (mem_sectionSpan_iff f U x).1 hx
  rw [map_sum]
  refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [map_mul, globalSectionVal_map]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (globalSectionVal_mem_sectionSpan f i V)

/-- **The objectwise ideal generated by `f_1, …, f_r`**, as a submodule of the underlying
presheaf of modules of the structure sheaf. Its membership condition is *not* local, which is
why the sheaf of ideals generated by the `f_i` is its closure and not itself. -/
def presheafGeneratedIdeal :
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val.Submodule where
  obj U := sectionSpan f U
  map {_ _} g _ hx := map_mem_sectionSpan f g hx

/-- Membership in the objectwise ideal, read as a submodule of the presheaf of modules, is
membership in the ideal of sections. -/
theorem mem_presheafGeneratedIdeal_iff (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.O.obj.obj U) :
    x ∈ (presheafGeneratedIdeal f).obj U ↔ x ∈ sectionSpan f U := Iff.rfl

/-- The objectwise ideal is the smallest objectwise submodule containing the values of the
generators. -/
theorem presheafGeneratedIdeal_le
    {N : (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val.Submodule}
    (h : ∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ N.obj U) :
    presheafGeneratedIdeal f ≤ N := fun U x hx ↦ by
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (mem_sectionSpan_iff f U x).1 ((mem_presheafGeneratedIdeal_iff f U x).1 hx)
  exact sum_mem fun i _ ↦ (N.obj U).smul_mem (c i) (h i U)

end Objectwise

section GeneratedIdealSheaf

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The sheaf of ideals `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪` generated by finitely many global sections of
the structure sheaf of a ringed site.** It is the smallest sheaf of ideals whose sections over
every object contain the `𝒪`-linear combinations of the values of `f_1, …, f_r` there; its
sections are described locally by `mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff`.

This is the `ℐ` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] and of [Stacks, Tag 099F]. -/
def generatedIdealSheaf :
    SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule (presheafGeneratedIdeal f)

/-- Every `𝒪`-linear combination of the values of the generators over an object is a section of
`ℐ` there. -/
theorem mem_generatedIdealSheaf_of_mem_sectionSpan {U : X.Cᵒᵖ} {x : X.O.obj.obj U}
    (hx : x ∈ sectionSpan f U) : x ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj U :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.le_sheafifySubmodule _ U hx

/-- **The generators are sections of the ideal sheaf they generate**, over every object of the
site. -/
theorem globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj U :=
  mem_generatedIdealSheaf_of_mem_sectionSpan f (globalSectionVal_mem_sectionSpan f i U)

/-- **The generators are sections of `ℐ`**, in the spelling in which consumers carry that fact as
a hypothesis on an arbitrary sheaf of ideals: for every object `U` of the site, the value of `f_i`
over `U` lies in `ℐ.toSubmodule.obj (op U)`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion` leaves the sheaf
of ideals free, so `IsDerivedComplete X I K` says nothing about the sections `f_i` unless they
belong to `I`; a statement about the Čech candidate therefore carries this as a hypothesis, and
at `I = generatedIdealSheaf f` it is discharged here. -/
theorem forall_globalSectionVal_mem_toSubmodule_generatedIdealSheaf (i : Fin r) (U : X.C) :
    globalSectionVal (f i) (op U) ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSubmodule.obj (op U) :=
  globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f i (op U)

/-- **`ℐ` is the smallest sheaf of ideals containing the generators.** Together with
`globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf` this characterises it, so it agrees with every other
construction of the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`. -/
theorem generatedIdealSheaf_le
    {𝓙 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (h : ∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ 𝓙.obj U) :
    generatedIdealSheaf f ≤ 𝓙 :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule_le (presheafGeneratedIdeal_le f h)

/-- Two sheaves of ideals each containing the generators and each least among those containing
them are equal: the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is unique. -/
theorem eq_generatedIdealSheaf
    {𝓙 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (hmem : ∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ 𝓙.obj U)
    (hle : ∀ 𝓚 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))),
      (∀ (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ 𝓚.obj U) → 𝓙 ≤ 𝓚) :
    𝓙 = generatedIdealSheaf f :=
  le_antisymm (hle _ (globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f))
    (generatedIdealSheaf_le f hmem)

/-- **The local description of `ℐ`.** A section of `𝒪` over `V` lies in the ideal sheaf
generated by `f_1, …, f_r` exactly when there is a covering sieve of `V` along every arrow of
which it becomes an `𝒪`-linear combination of the generators.

This is the warning of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] made precise: membership in `ℐ` is local, so a section
of `ℐ` over `V` need not itself be a combination of the `f_i`. -/
theorem mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff {V : X.Cᵒᵖ} {x : X.O.obj.obj V} :
    x ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj V ↔
      ∃ S : Sieve V.unop, S ∈ X.J V.unop ∧
        ∀ ⦃W : X.C⦄ (g : W ⟶ V.unop), S g →
          ∃ c : Fin r → X.O.obj.obj (op W),
            ∑ i, c i * globalSectionVal (f i) (op W) = (X.O.obj.map g.op).hom x :=
  Iff.trans Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff
    (exists_congr fun _ ↦ and_congr_right fun _ ↦
      ⟨fun h _ g hg ↦ (mem_sectionSpan_iff f _ _).1 (h g hg),
        fun h _ g hg ↦ (mem_sectionSpan_iff f _ _).2 (h g hg)⟩)

/-- A section which is locally an `𝒪`-linear combination of the generators is a section of
`ℐ`. -/
theorem mem_generatedIdealSheaf_of_locally {V : X.Cᵒᵖ} {x : X.O.obj.obj V}
    {S : Sieve V.unop} (hS : S ∈ X.J V.unop)
    (hx : ∀ ⦃W : X.C⦄ (g : W ⟶ V.unop), S g →
      ∃ c : Fin r → X.O.obj.obj (op W),
        ∑ i, c i * globalSectionVal (f i) (op W) = (X.O.obj.map g.op).hom x) :
    x ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj V :=
  (mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff f).2 ⟨S, hS, hx⟩

/-- A section of `ℐ` over `V` becomes an `𝒪`-linear combination of the generators along every
arrow of some covering sieve of `V`. -/
theorem exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf {V : X.Cᵒᵖ} {x : X.O.obj.obj V}
    (hx : x ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj V) :
    ∃ S : Sieve V.unop, S ∈ X.J V.unop ∧
      ∀ ⦃W : X.C⦄ (g : W ⟶ V.unop), S g →
        ∃ c : Fin r → X.O.obj.obj (op W),
          ∑ i, c i * globalSectionVal (f i) (op W) = (X.O.obj.map g.op).hom x :=
  (mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff f).1 hx

end GeneratedIdealSheaf

section Consumers

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}

/-- Evaluation at an object of a compatible family of local sections of the structure sheaf, as
a ring homomorphism. -/
def sectionsEval (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj →+*
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U :=
  (Pi.evalRingHom _ U).comp
    (RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj).subtype

/-- **A compatible family of local sections of the structure sheaf, read as a global section**
in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 06UN]. The two spellings of a global section both occur in this
directory: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor` is indexed by
`Presheaf.globalSections`, while `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy` consumes
`RingCat.sectionsSubring`. -/
def globalSectionOfSections
    (s : RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj) :
    Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm ⟨s.1, fun g ↦ s.2 g⟩

/-- The value over `U` of `globalSectionOfSections s` is the component `s.1 U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSections
    (s : RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfSections (X := X) s) U = s.1 U := by
  unfold globalSectionVal globalSectionOfSections
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- **A section of the structure sheaf over a terminal object of the site, read as a global
section.** On a site with a terminal object `T` the two notions agree, a compatible family being
determined by its value over `T`; this is the form in which a "global section" is given on the
site of opens of a ringed space, as a section over `⊤`. -/
def globalSectionOfTerminalSection {T : X.C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (s : X.O.obj.obj (op T)) :
    Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm
    ⟨fun U ↦ (X.O.obj.map (hT.from U.unop).op).hom s, fun {U V} g ↦ by
      change (X.O.obj.map g).hom ((X.O.obj.map (hT.from U.unop).op).hom s) = _
      rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← X.O.obj.map_comp,
        show (hT.from U.unop).op ≫ g = (hT.from V.unop).op from
          Quiver.Hom.unop_inj (hT.hom_ext _ _)]⟩

/-- The value over `U` of `globalSectionOfTerminalSection hT s` is the restriction of `s` along
the unique map from `U` to the terminal object `T`. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection {T : X.C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (s : X.O.obj.obj (op T)) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfTerminalSection hT s) U =
      (X.O.obj.map (hT.from U.unop).op).hom s := by
  unfold globalSectionVal globalSectionOfTerminalSection
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- **The hypothesis `IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy` of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] is satisfiable.** For an
ideal `I = (a_1, …, a_r)` of a ring `A` mapping to the global sections of `𝒪`, the sheaf of
ideals generated by the images of the `a_i` is the ideal sheaf `I𝒪` generated by `I`: it
contains the local sections of every global section coming from `I`, and is least among the
sheaves of ideals that do.

Every finitely generated ideal is of this form, so the hypothesis
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy` that
`exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` carries is now produced rather than assumed. -/
theorem isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
    (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
    {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A) :
    IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A (Ideal.span (Set.range a)) X ρ
      (generatedIdealSheaf fun i ↦ globalSectionOfSections (ρ (a i))) := by
  refine ⟨fun b U hb ↦ ?_, fun 𝓙 h𝓙 ↦ generatedIdealSheaf_le _ fun i U ↦ ?_⟩
  · refine mem_generatedIdealSheaf_of_mem_sectionSpan _ ?_
    refine (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_ : Ideal.span (Set.range a) ≤
      Ideal.comap ((sectionsEval U).comp ρ)
        (sectionSpan (fun i ↦ globalSectionOfSections (ρ (a i))) U)) hb
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact globalSectionVal_mem_sectionSpan (fun i ↦ globalSectionOfSections (ρ (a i))) i U
  · rw [globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSections]
    exact h𝓙 (a i) U (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)

/-- **For `I ⊂ A` finitely generated, `I𝒪` is generated by finitely many global sections of
`𝒪`.** `Ideal.FG` writes `I = (a_1, …, a_r)`, and then the global sections `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` of
`𝒪` generate `I𝒪`, by `isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf`.

Finite generation of `I` is the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] itself, so this says that the
global sections are there for nothing: the ideal sheaf along which the source forms `ℱ^∧` is
always one of the `generatedIdealSheaf f`. -/
theorem exists_generatedIdealSheaf_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
    (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
    {I : Ideal A} (hI : I.FG) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})),
      IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ (generatedIdealSheaf f) := by
  obtain ⟨r, a, rfl⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.1 hI
  exact ⟨r, _, isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf A X ρ a⟩

/-- **Every `I𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] is a `generatedIdealSheaf`.** For `I ⊂ A` finitely
generated — the source's own hypothesis — an ideal sheaf `𝓘` is `I𝒪` only if it *is* the ideal
sheaf generated by `r` global sections of `𝒪`, for some `r`.

This is `exists_generatedIdealSheaf_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy` together with the uniqueness of
`I𝒪`, `eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy`. Its consequence for this directory is that "the ideal
sheaf `I𝒪` is generated by finitely many **global** sections of `𝒪`" is no restriction on the
data of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX]: a theorem proved for `generatedIdealSheaf f` at an arbitrary `r` and
an arbitrary `f` applies, after rewriting along this equality, to every `(A, I, 𝒞, 𝒪, ρ, 𝓘)`
satisfying the source's hypotheses. In particular
`exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated.lean` is at the source's generality, and so is the regime of
`PushforwardCommutesCompletionGenerated.lean`. The genuinely restricted regime of this directory
is the other one, nilpotence of the local sections of `𝓘`, which is a condition on `𝓘` that most
ideal sheaves fail. -/
theorem exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
    (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
    {I : Ideal A} (hI : I.FG)
    {𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (h𝓘 : IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ 𝓘) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})),
      𝓘 = generatedIdealSheaf f :=
  let ⟨r, f, hf⟩ := exists_generatedIdealSheaf_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy A X ρ hI
  ⟨r, f, eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ h𝓘 hf⟩

/-- **The generation hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] is satisfiable over a terminal object.**
Over a terminal object `U` of the site, the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is generated
as an ideal sheaf by their values over `U`, in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver`.

A terminal object is needed, and only for one step: that predicate asks a local section of `𝓘`
over an arbitrary object `V` to become, locally on `V`, a combination of the *restrictions along
some arrow `W ⟶ U`* of the chosen sections. For a global section the restriction is the value,
so the content is `exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf`; what is not automatic is that the
arrow `W ⟶ U` exists at all, and over a terminal object it does. This is a property of the
*site*, not of the ideal sheaf: on a site with no terminal object the predicate is not satisfied
by any ideal sheaf with a non-zero section over an object admitting no arrow to `U`. -/
theorem isGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver_generatedIdealSheaf
    {X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}} {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
    (U : X.C) (hU : IsTerminal U) :
    IsGeneratedAsIdealSheafBySectionsOver X (generatedIdealSheaf f) U
      fun i ↦ globalSectionVal (f i) (op U) := by
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f i (op U), fun V s hs ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hc⟩ := exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f hs
  refine ⟨S, hS, fun W g hg ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hcw⟩ := hc g hg
  refine ⟨hU.from W, c, ?_⟩
  have key : ∑ i, c i * (X.O.obj.map (hU.from W).op).hom (globalSectionVal (f i) (op U))
      = ∑ i, c i * globalSectionVal (f i) (op W) :=
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by rw [globalSectionVal_map]
  exact (key.trans hcw).symm

end Consumers

section Generators

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The map out of a free sheaf of modules determined by a family of sections takes the
tautological section of the `i`-th summand to the `i`-th section of the family: the composite of
`SheafOfModules.ιFree i` with it is, by the definition of `SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv`, the map
`𝒪 ⟶ M` named by the `i`-th section, and such a map is recovered from its value at `1`. -/
theorem freeHomEquiv_symm_val_app_one {M : SheafOfModules.{w} R} {I : Type w}
    (s : I → M.sections) (i : I) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (M.freeHomEquiv.symm s).val.app U
        ((SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := R) i).val.app U (1 : R.obj.obj U)) = (s i).val U := by
  have h : M.unitHomEquiv (SheafOfModules.ιFree i ≫ M.freeHomEquiv.symm s) = s i :=
    congrFun (M.freeHomEquiv.apply_symm_apply s) i
  exact ((M.unitHomEquiv_apply_coe (SheafOfModules.ιFree i ≫ M.freeHomEquiv.symm s) U).symm.trans
    (congrArg (fun t : M.sections ↦ t.val U) h))

end Generators

section GeneratingSections

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- The value over `U` of the `i`-th generator, as a section of `ℐ` there. -/
def generatorVal (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) : (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj U :=
  ⟨globalSectionVal (f i) U, globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f i U⟩

/-- The underlying section of `𝒪` of `generatorVal f i U` is the value of `f i` over `U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatorVal_coe (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    (generatorVal f i U).1 = globalSectionVal (f i) U := rfl

/-- **The `i`-th generator, as a global section of the sheaf of ideals it generates.** -/
def generatorSection (i : Fin r) : (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules.sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (generatorVal f i)
    fun _ _ g ↦ Subtype.ext (globalSectionVal_map (f i) g)

/-- The value over `U` of the global section `generatorSection f i` is `generatorVal f i U`. -/
theorem generatorSection_val (i : Fin r) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    (generatorSection f i).val U = generatorVal f i U := rfl

/-- **The map `𝒪^r ⟶ ℐ` named by the generators.** -/
def generatingSectionsHom :
    SheafOfModules.free (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (ULift.{w} (Fin r)) ⟶
      (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules :=
  (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv.symm fun i ↦ generatorSection f i.down

/-- **`𝒪^r ⟶ ℐ` is locally surjective.** This is the local description of `ℐ`, read as a
statement about the map named by the generators: a section of `ℐ` over `V` becomes, along every
arrow of a covering sieve, the image of the section `∑ c_i e_i` of `𝒪^r`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_generatingSectionsHom :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective X.J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj).map
        (generatingSectionsHom f).val) := by
  refine ⟨fun {V} s ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hc⟩ := exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f s.2
  refine X.J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦ ?_) hS
  obtain ⟨c₀, hcw⟩ := hc g hg
  let c : Fin r → ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op W) := fun i ↦ c₀ i
  refine ⟨∑ i : Fin r, c i •
    (SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
      (ULift.up i)).val.app (op W)
        (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op W)), ?_⟩
  have key : ((generatingSectionsHom f).val.app (op W)).hom
        (∑ i : Fin r, c i •
          (SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
            (ULift.up i)).val.app (op W)
              (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj (op W)))
      = ∑ i : Fin r, c i • generatorVal f i (op W) := by
    rw [map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [map_smul]
    exact congrArg (c i • ·) (freeHomEquiv_symm_val_app_one _ (ULift.up i) (op W))
  have final : (∑ i : Fin r, c i • generatorVal f i (op W))
      = (((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj).obj
          (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules.val).map g.op) s := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    rw [Submodule.coe_sum]
    refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_) hcw
    rw [Submodule.coe_smul]
    rfl
  exact key.trans final

/-- **`ℐ` is generated by `r` global sections**, [Stacks, Tag 01B4] for the ideal sheaf
generated by `f_1, …, f_r`: the map `𝒪^r ⟶ ℐ` named by the generators is an epimorphism,
because it is locally surjective. -/
def generatingSections : (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules.GeneratingSections where
  I := ULift.{w} (Fin r)
  s i := generatorSection f i.down
  epi := Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _
    (isLocallySurjective_generatingSectionsHom f)

/-- **The generating family of `ℐ` is finite**, of cardinality `r`. This is the finite-type
content of [Stacks, Tag 099B]'s hypothesis on `ℐ`, at the generality of an arbitrary ringed
site; see the module documentation for why `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` itself is a statement
about the site as well. -/
instance isFiniteType_generatingSections : (generatingSections f).IsFiniteType where
  finite := inferInstanceAs (Finite (ULift.{w} (Fin r)))

/-- **`ℐ` is of finite type** in the sense of `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, on a site over which
that predicate can be unwound. The three instance hypotheses are hypotheses on the *site*, not on
the ideal sheaf: `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` asks for a covering of the terminal object
together with finite generating sections of the restriction of `ℐ` to each member's slice site,
and `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.localGeneratorsData` — which produces that data from
global generators, using the trivial covering by every object — carries them. On a general ringed
site the statement available is `generatingSections` itself, which is stronger where both are
defined: `ℐ` is generated by `r` sections over the whole site. -/
theorem isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf [HasBinaryProducts X.C]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] :
    (generatedIdealSheaf f).toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType := by
  constructor
  exact ⟨(generatingSections f).localGeneratorsData,
    { isFiniteType := fun _ ↦ ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite (ULift.{w} (Fin r)))⟩ }⟩

end GeneratingSections

section Completion

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099F] for the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, at that ideal sheaf
itself.** This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion`
with the sheaf of ideals no longer a free parameter: it is the `ℐ` of [Stacks, Tag 099B],
generated by the very sections the Čech complex is built from. The three hypotheses are the
three remaining properties of the Čech completion functor, exactly as in `Completion.lean`;
what this statement removes is the arbitrariness of the ideal sheaf, which is why 099B and 099F
could previously not be stated at their own hypotheses.

The three hypotheses are *not* discharged here and this declaration carries no tag; the roadmap
for them is the module documentation of `Completion.lean`. The `hη` argument is available:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`
of `CompletionUnitInvertible.lean`, which is also where the two-hypothesis form of this
statement, with `hη` already supplied, lives. -/
theorem isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_generatedIdealSheaf
    (hΦ : ∀ K, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f)
      ((completionFunctor X f).obj K))
    (hη : ∀ K, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f) K →
      IsIso ((completionUnit X f).app K))
    (hcomm : ∀ K, (completionFunctor X f).map ((completionUnit X f).app K) =
      (completionUnit X f).app ((completionFunctor X f).obj K)) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (generatedIdealSheaf f))).IsRightAdjoint :=
  isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion X f (generatedIdealSheaf f) hΦ hη hcomm

end Completion

